.TH SDL_MouseMotionTransformCallback 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_MouseMotionTransformCallback \- A callback used to transform mouse motion delta from raw values.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_mouse.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef void (SDLCALL *SDL_MouseMotionTransformCallback)( void *userdata, Uint64 timestamp, SDL_Window *window, SDL_MouseID mouseID, float *x, float *y);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is called during SDL\(aqs handling of platform mouse events to scale the values of the resulting motion delta\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I userdata
what was passed as
.BR userdata
to
.BR SDL_SetRelativeMouseTransform ()\[char46]

.TP
.I timestamp
the associated time at which this mouse motion event was received\[char46]
.TP
.I window
the associated window to which this mouse motion event was addressed\[char46]
.TP
.I mouseID
the associated mouse from which this mouse motion event was emitted\[char46]
.TP
.I x
pointer to a variable that will be treated as the resulting x-axis motion\[char46]
.TP
.I y
pointer to a variable that will be treated as the resulting y-axis motion\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
This callback is called by SDL\(aqs internal mouse input processing procedure, which may be a thread separate from the main event loop that is run at realtime priority\[char46] Stalling this thread with too much work in the callback can therefore potentially freeze the entire system\[char46] Care should be taken with proper synchronization practices when adding other side effects beyond mutation of the x and y values\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetRelativeMouseTransform (3)
